    readTime: '23 min read',
    intro: `App design is the discipline of creating digital products that users carry with them everywhere and interact with dozens of times per day. Unlike websites, which users visit with a specific goal and then leave, mobile apps become habitual tools woven into daily routines — the alarm app that starts the morning, the navigation app that guides the commute, the messaging app that maintains relationships. This intimacy creates both enormous opportunity and serious responsibility: a well-designed app genuinely improves how people spend their time, while a poorly designed one wastes it. App design encompasses everything from the information architecture that structures content, to the visual design that creates identity and clarity, to the micro-interactions that make every tap feel responsive and satisfying. Understanding it as a discipline requires moving past the notion that design is decoration and embracing it as a systematic practice of solving problems for real people with real constraints. This guide builds the foundational mental model for professional app design.`,
