    intro: `Usability testing — observing real users attempting to use an app — is among the most valuable activities in app design, and one of the most underused. The fundamental truth that usability testing addresses is that designers cannot see their own designs as users do. The designer knows how the app is meant to work, understands its structure, and cannot un-know these things to experience the app as a new user does. Real users, encountering the app fresh, reveal the problems the designer cannot see — the confusions, the missteps, the points where the design fails to communicate. A small amount of usability testing reveals problems that no amount of internal review would find, and it does so cheaply and quickly. Yet many teams skip it, relying on their own judgment, and ship apps with problems that testing would have caught. This guide covers usability testing for mobile apps: why it matters, how to conduct it, and how to turn its findings into better apps.`,
